  "Question": "The median of the list\n\n\\[ \\begin{gathered} n,\\ n+3,\\ n+4,\\ n+5,\\ n+6, \\\\ \\ n+8,\\ n+10,\\ n+12,\\ n+15 \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nis \\(10.\\) What is the mean?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(11\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The entries are already in increasing order, because adding the same \\(n\\) to the increasing offsets preserves their order. With nine entries, the median is the fifth entry, so\n\\[\nn+6=10,\\qquad n=4.\n\\]\nSubstituting gives the list \\(4,7,8,9,10,12,14,16,19\\). Its mean is its sum divided by nine:\n\\[\n\\frac{4+7+8+9+10+12+14+16+19}{9}\n=\\frac{99}{9}=11.\n\\]\nThe mean is \\(\\boxed{11}\\), choice E.",
